{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"No. Appointing a principal underwriter does **not** itself assure a sales force, meaningful promotion, intermediary access, or asset gathering.\n\nFor a registered fund, the principal underwriter is the entity that distributes fund shares as principal or acts as the fund’s agent in their distribution. That role supports the ETF’s **legal and operational distribution**—for example, handling share sales and related distribution arrangements. It does not imply a dedicated sales team or a commitment to market the ETF.\n\nMarketing, wholesaling, platform placement, and access to broker-dealer or adviser channels may require **separate contracts, services, and fees**. What a series-trust sponsor or service provider includes varies by package; some offer more support, while others provide only core fund and distribution infrastructure. Review the governing documents and service agreements for the specific ETF rather than infer sales coverage from the underwriter appointment."}}
